cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Dark Synth, cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Dark Synth: A Tag-Audited Methodology for Mathematical Work, with a Kernel-Verified Catalytic Pass Barrier"
version: 1.2.2
date-released: 2026-10-27
abstract: >
  A tag-audited methodology for mathematical work. Every claim carries a
  two-axis [source/status] tag; every correction is logged in an append-only
  hash-chained ledger; every [run] claim is kernel-accepted with a sha256
  binding; the audit trail is tested against its own mutants. The reference
  vault contains Theorem 3.6 (Coq 8.18, interpolation barrier r >= D+1 for
  the class C_int) and Theorem 3.7 (Lean 4.7.0, the same barrier over any
  commutative ring including Z_m with zero divisors).
